{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_297","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1791304223243-compiler-engineer-ucf-d14-source.findings.md | tail -65; rg -n '\"'^FAIL|''^ERROR'\"' /private/tmp/d14-full-fast-escalated.log | tail -8; rg -n 'SKIP|WARNING|FAIL|ERROR' /private/tmp/d14-ruling-full-jvm-final3.log | tail -12\"","aggregated_output":"\n## Whole-task contract audit\n\n| Contract | What the partial implementation has right | Remaining defects / incomplete work |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. Export entry, fork, prepare, encode | Uses landed enter/prepare/encode; preserves the live returned record during retries. Nil arbitration follows the version-0 fork path without minting custody or sending an offer. | Durable state is not the complete export record. Fresh-process restoration loses saved waits, bindings and retained operations. Existing recovery coverage does not prove the fenced fresh-machine case. |\n| 2. Mint once before prepare | Journals the mint before prepare; initializes source custody with counter zero/no origin; derives successor custody from the current occurrence; stores before the fenced marker. | The stored object is only a projection, not the complete prepared record. Cuts around preparation cannot recover all required state. |\n| 3. Write-ahead brackets and stable proposals | Writes initial offer/proposal/resumed/release intents before sending. Journals the proposal id before sending. Uses front reply-evidence identity checks before recording acknowledgment. | Source reopen ignores an actually sent journaled proposal, losing its stable id. Candidate recovery loses acknowledged proposal progress and may lack arbitration without a mint. Intent selection iterates a map rather than journal order. Enrollment recovery loses its intents/outcomes. |\n| 4. Abort depends on journaled attempts | Delegates closed refusal-family and tenure checks to the landed abort path. | The offer bracket does not record a new intent before each retry. An uncertain successful retry can be omitted from attempt history, permitting abort after possible admission. A direct probe reproduced `:stalled` -> `:aborted`, gate `:running`. Abort also uses original grant time rather than successful renewal basis, conservatively rejecting some still-valid tenure. |\n| 5. Exit brackets, exit cuts, halt | Normal successor/result paths use the landed completion/report/release mechanism; halted results are stored and terminal closure is delegated to authority. | Exit recovery can select old resumed/release intents without matching the current lease/origin. An old acknowledgment can suppress a new release. A minted-but-unfenced exit falls into holder recovery instead of retaining its current export record. Closure matching and boundary-cut coverage are insufficient. The offer-admission ordering requires the ruling noted above. |\n| 6. Tenure through exit | Safepoint/exit paths retain renewal/recheck logic; D13 direct-effect guards remain. | `step-active-held` drains before its local-bound check and can apply an acknowledgment at the bound (existing red test). Export serve/store/offer/report actions lack per-action tenure checks after computation/preparation. Reopened exits do not reconstruct a sufficient holder clock/renewal basis for subsequent IO. |\n| 7. Reopen reconciliation | Has explicit source, exit and holder recovery branches and retains journal/storage handles. | Complete saved state is absent; supplied original machine is assumed. Missing body/recovery cases can fall through to preparation or the wrong branch instead of failing closed. The required fresh-process reconstruction is blocked by the missing seam. |\n| 8. Uncertain append stops progress | `step` catches the uncertain-append marker, stalls, and subsequent `step` leaves that state unchanged. | Public `abort` and `enroll` are not guarded against stalled state. Direct enrollment does not catch the marker into stalled state. Journal reads treat every non-ok response as end-of-history, which can accept a truncated prefix after transport failure. |\n| 9. Holder recovery | An accepted journaled grant can be recovered without a machine, released, and followed by candidacy. The admitted-lower variant is retained. | Release selection is not bound to the current lease; historical grants/exit markers can override later progress. Stable proposal replay is incomplete. Fresh-prefix recovery needs tests proving no program execution or attachment before acceptance. |\n| 10. C12 enrollment discipline | Journals a derived target before the first enrollment call. Can acknowledge an uncertain reply when a fresh authenticated projection already shows commitment. | Retries call the enrollment seam before reconciliation, allowing duplicate enrollment. Reopen drops enrollment progress. A probe observed two calls and three total targets (the original target plus two new targets). |\n| 11. Run-end semantics / residual 2 | Contains root/child end handling, stopped-program cleanup, release obligations and one-diagnostic handling, without fabricating completion or resetting authority quarantine. | The divergence fixture changes `entry :stream-id` while resolution still uses the cursor cell, so it is not a real divergence; accepting stale does not prove the intended row. The intent-conflict fixture fails before activation because its enrolled retained write has no id. True replay-divergence/conflict, no-successor, release/regrant and quarantine rows remain incomplete. |\n\nThe runtime step state still contains composition functions, live machines and resolver/seam objects. Journal records are mostly plain data, but a literal plain-data driver-state contract remains unmet; environment/state separation needs an agreed API rather than an incidental rewrite.\n\n## Diagnostic evidence\n\nTemporary probes were written only to `/private/tmp/d14-audit-probes.clj`, using existing test fixture helpers, not private landed implementation helpers. They are diagnostics, not repository tests or assertion counts.\n\nCommand: `clj -Sdeps '{:aliases {:probe {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:probe /private/tmp/d14-audit-probes.clj` — exit 0; output `/private/tmp/d14-audit-probes2.log`.\n\n1. Canonical complete-record encoding: unsupported `yin.vm.values.Closure`.\n2. Fresh-machine fenced reopen: `{:saved-waits 1 :restored-waits 0 :restored-gate nil :stored-keys (:header :served)}`.\n3. Sent source proposal then reopen: non-nil proposal id before recovery, nil afterward, phase `:exporting`.\n4. Folding offer intent, full attempt, then unmatched retry intent retains only the known full attempt, losing the unknown attempt.\n5. Crash after a successful retry send but before its attempt record: two sends, before `:stalled`, after public abort `:aborted`, gate `:running`.\n6. Uncertain committed enrollment followed by temporarily unavailable ledger: two enrollment seam calls, phase `:exporting`, three targets.\n\n## Tests and checks — exact outcomes\n\n### Focused driver suite\n\n`clj -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver-test`\n\n**48 tests, 490 assertions, 24 failures, 1 error; exit 1.** Log: `/private/tmp/d14-baseline.log`.\n\nFailures include actual late acknowledgment application at the tenure bound and broken source proposal recovery. Several inherited rows also make invalid phase/count assumptions: first mint/fence is the source rather than the result; whole journal contains source/proposal records rather than only exit records; five steps do not yet send the proposed id; immediate authenticated enrollment observation may legitimately acknowledge commitment. The abort fixture expects abort after inbound acceptance plus authority refusal, contradicting the journaled-attempt rule. The error is the intent-conflict fixture's `:unprotected-pending` refusal before holder activation. These need test-first corrections, not assertions weakened to fit the partial implementation.\n\n### Full JVM fast lane\n\nCompleted command: `bb test:clj > /private/tmp/d14-full-fast-escalated.log`\n\n**3529 tests, 234739 assertions, 25 failures, 1 error; exit 1.** The driver accounts for 24 failures and the error. The additional failure is `yin.vm.store-write-audit-test/every-store-mutation-is-on-the-allowlist`, detecting `driver.cljc`'s `bare-state` literal `:store` association. That slot holds the composition content byte-store, but is flagged by the store mutation auditor. This is introduced by the partial D14 implementation, not an unrelated pre-existing failure. An internal slot rename may resolve it within scope; changing the allowlist would be outside scope. Neither was changed after the stop condition.\n\nAn earlier sandbox run (`/private/tmp/d14-full-fast.log`) compiled 184 Node REPL files (183 compiled, zero warnings) and completed pinned ANTLR generation, then encountered Babashka shutdown `sysctl` permission errors. It was interrupted (exit 130) before aggregate test results. It is not counted as a completed suite. The approved rerun above produced the full counts.\n\nFast-lane skips: missing Dart WS peer `build/ws-project-peer`, missing Dart REPL peer `build/yin-repl-peer`, and host-inapplicable CBOR cases. Slow tests were excluded by the fast-lane definition. No dedicated Dart or Node driver suite was run in this continuation.\n\nPrerequisite installation: approved `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund`, exit 0, 69 packages added in 792 ms; log `/private/tmp/d14-npm-ci.log`. No lifecycle scripts or tracked package/lock edits.\n\n### Static checks\n\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc`: **0 errors, 6 warnings, exit 2**, `/private/tmp/d14-kondo.log`. Unused: `acked?` (source 513), `units` (source 2233), `w` (test 1975), `l` (test 2221), `h` (test 2398), `s3` (test 2578).\n- `cljstyle --no-color check` on both files: **2 incorrectly formatted files, exit 2**, `/private/tmp/d14-style.log`. It ran; it was not sandbox-blocked.\n- `git diff --check`: **exit 0**, `/private/tmp/d14-diff-check.log`.\n\n## Red/green status and remaining work\n\nThis continuation produced red baseline evidence and concrete diagnostic reproductions, not a green implementation result. No repository regression tests were added or fixed, and no test-first implementation cycle is claimed. The inherited partial changes remain 1532 insertions/176 deletions in the driver and 863 insertions/14 deletions in its test file. The requested report is the only new file.\n\nAfter the seam/ruling is resolved, the remaining test-first work includes complete-record/fresh-machine recovery, every prepare/fence/intent/send/ack cut, stable proposal replay after send and answer, lease-matched exit recovery, retry uncertainty preventing abort, public stalled-entry guards, fail-closed journal reads, enrollment reconciliation before retry and across reopen, tenure at each exit IO boundary, and genuine residual-2 conflict/divergence/run-end rows. Then repair the audit slot and formatting/lint issues and rerun both suites. D14 is not complete and must not be merged as ready on this evidence.\n662:FAIL in (a-holder-aborts-a-hand-off-only-with-tenure-test) (driver_test.cljc:2521)\n666:FAIL in (a-holder-aborts-a-hand-off-only-with-tenure-test) (driver_test.cljc:2528)\n671:FAIL in (an-uncertain-journal-append-stalls-the-driver-test) (driver_test.cljc:2110)\n677:FAIL in (an-uncertain-journal-append-stalls-the-driver-test) (driver_test.cljc:2114)\n683:FAIL in (a-crash-between-proposal-send-and-answer-resends-the-stable-id-test) (driver_test.cljc:2058)\n687:FAIL in (a-crash-between-proposal-send-and-answer-resends-the-stable-id-test) (driver_test.cljc:529)\n692:FAIL in (a-crash-between-proposal-send-and-answer-resends-the-stable-id-test) (driver_test.cljc:2065)\n696:FAIL in (a-crash-between-proposal-send-and-answer-resends-the-stable-id-test) (driver_test.cljc:2066)\n13:WARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n66:SKIP jvm coll/set-signed-zero-collapse: host constructor merged the members (N/A; cbor-v1.errata.md E1)\n67:SKIP jvm coll/set-decimal-scale-collapse: host constructor merged the members (N/A; cbor-v1.errata.md E1)\n68:SKIP jvm coll/set-vector-list-collapse: host constructor merged the members (N/A; cbor-v1.errata.md E1)\n69:SKIP jvm coll/map-integer-width-duplicate: host constructor merged the members (N/A; cbor-v1.errata.md E1)\n70:SKIP jvm num/js-unsafe-integer: README Obligations: applies to Node only; N/A on JVM and Dart\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
